// ROUND THREE B: THE CROP'S EDGE IS ITS OWN LINE, NOT THE LIP'S TEETH. The old bare band was a sum of stepped waves of the
// angle (bays three metres across with upright sides, nine metres apart): from the field they were SQUARE TEETH of gold
// over a dark gap. Now the lip's line (lipBite) breaks in round scallops and a few slips, never in steps, and the crop
// ends on a line of its own that wanders slowly behind it (cropBack: 4.4 m behind the lip's line, a little more where
// the cave is deep, 3 m more round the wheel's bite, swaying 0.7 m in twenty and 0.3 m in eight), from the cut front
// south to 0.8 of a radian, easing back to the lip from there to 1.0: between the two lies A SHOULDER OF BARE EARTH
// two to five metres broad (lipBare; nearly eight by the wheel), which a metre of standing crop cannot hide from the
// flight. Sines only; the shaders' lipBiteG is cropBack's own sum, fd_tearG is lipBite's.
// (ROUND THREE D, fc: THE STAND STOPS FARTHER BACK AWAY FROM THE WHEEL'S OWN BITE. From the look back the lens is BEHIND
