    // (ROUND THREE C: STRAW GOLD, CLEARLY WARM, never cream or grey: the stubs' own colour and the earth's are warmer
    // and hold far off as near; AND STREAKS OF THICKER AND THINNER STUBS a metre broad and some fifteen long along the
    // drill's way, THERE FROM NEAR AND FAR ALIKE (the mend after round three c's reader: they were brought in only
    // between 0.1 and 1.6 m of footprint, a thing a metre broad coming and going with the distance): gone to their
    // mean, nothing, only as their own breadth goes under the pixel (whole to 0.25 m of footprint, gone by 0.55, half
    // the 1.1 m cell); and each pass of the combine a twentieth lighter or darker than the next, eased, as the stubs lean with its going)
