  // (THE CLOUDS' SHADOWS IN THE PIT: pitCloud, with the field's own cloudCutL: the land, the crop and what lies on the land all have it)
  // (NO POOLS, round three b: poolD and its gates are gone; the floor asks no pool's shore)
  // THE PIT'S OWN SHADOW: how much of the sun the pit's far sides (the south and the west) take from a place in it: the
  // sun's ray is tried against the three kerbs (11 m, 22 m and the lip). flp: the flare at the place's own angle (near
  // the bay, where it is small, the sun comes in over the open south-west and nothing is tried)
