  // across them: each rut a shallow trough with a wall each side)
  // (ROUND THREE D: A RUT IS PRESSED, AND THE EARTH IT PRESSED OUT STANDS BESIDE IT: a squeezed bank each side of
  // each trough, 0.35 m broad and a hand high (its outer slope 0.24), so that under the low sun each rut is a lit
  // bank, a shaded wall, a lit wall and a shaded bank side by side, 1.1 m in all: light and shade at the track's
  // own breadth, which holds as long as that breadth is a footprint; a dark line alone read as painted)
