      // THE SKIN OF LOOSE EARTH (a tipped heap, a berm, a windrow, the talus): RILLS run down its flanks; A DRY PALE
      // CRUST lies on the side that looks to the sun; FRESH DARK EARTH lies in tongues where it last slid; and LUMPS
      // sit on it, each a dome lit by its own slope with its shade behind it (pg_stone: the floor's own clods). All by
      // place: a rill and a slide are laid by the FOOT POINT of the fall line a place lies on (ft: the place moved
      // out down the heap's own slope to the ground; one point for the whole line), each fading to its mean as the
      // footprint outgrows it
