// AN OLD LIME OF THE SHELTER ROW (t: one of limeTrees()): a thick short stem; THE HEART, closed: a round bar of dark
// inner leaf LIMES.heart in radius about the stem from LIMES.lo to t.hi over the ground, its two ends round (a lathe of
// twelve sides and sixteen to the round: no line passes through it). ON THE HEART THE CROWN IS HEAPED IN BILLOWS, each
// a rounded mass of leaf three to seven metres across, a third to a half sunk in the heart: one at the top, t.up over the heart's own
